    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθέτ-ησις</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a setting aside, abolition</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμαρτίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Heb.</u>
					9.26
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				8.142
			</span></i>; '<i>annulling</i>' of a deed, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				2.142.24
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>rejection</i> (of a spurious passage), <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				5.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				3.66
			</span></i>; generally, <i>rejection</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐποχή</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				6.9.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>breach of faith</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				191.24
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
